      {
        "file": "platform/ci/wait_for.py",
        "issue": "--marker \"\" (or whitespace) matched the first blank line of the log, so wait_for reported a job done that was still running. Now an argparse error (exit 2); test_rejects_inputs_that_can_never_mean_done.",
        "patched": true
      },
      {
        "file": "platform/ci/wait_for.py",
        "issue": "--pid -1 made os.kill(-1, 0) probe every process, so it waited the full timeout and never reported done; --pid 0 was silently ignored and fell through to the log/--until path. Both are now argparse errors (exit 2).",
        "patched": true
      },
      {
        "file": "platform/ci/check_social_proof.py",
        "issue": "Attribution was searched across the whole line, and a minified page is one line, so any 'for example'/'such as'/'sample' anywhere on it excused every unbacked claim. Now attribution must sit within 120 characters of the claim.",
        "patched": true
      },
      {
        "file": "platform/ci/check_social_proof.py",
        "issue": "'Trusted&nbsp;by', 'As&nbsp;seen in', '&#160;' and U+00A0 hid claims from the pattern. Entities and NBSP now normalise to a space first.",
        "patched": true
      },
      {
        "file": "platform/ci/check_social_proof.py",
        "issue": "Inline tags between the words ('Trusted <b>by</b> 4,000 shops') hid claims. Inline tags (b, strong, em, span, a, ...) are now stripped first; <code> is kept, since it marks an example.",
        "patched": true
      },
      {
        "file": "platform/ci/check_social_proof.py",
        "issue": "'Award&#8209;winning' (non-breaking hyphen) escaped. Hyphen entities and U+2010/2011 now normalise to '-'.",
        "patched": true
      },
      {
        "file": "platform/ci/check_social_proof.py",
        "issue": "Abbreviated counts ('Join 10k+ freelancers', 'Join 1.2M users', '50K happy customers') escaped the join/happy patterns. They now accept a decimal and a k/m suffix.",
